From: Carlos Cabrera H. <6750732+ccabrerah@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 25] ggml-sycl: gathered sparse prefill attention for QSA (each query's chosen cells on DPAS)

GGML_SYCL_FUSE_SPARSE_PREFILL=1 (with the engine's graph order). A prompt chunk's QSA attention is a [n_kv, T] F16
selection mask (FILL -inf, SET_ROWS 0 at the indexer's cells, + causal) over a dense FLASH_ATTN_EXT, whose cost grows
with n_kv * T. Matched from the mask's FILL to the FA, it becomes one kernel per (query, kv head) over that query's
cells straight from the q8_0 cache, after vLLM's QSA kernel: the GQA group's heads are the matrix rows, so S = Q K^T and
O += P V run as joint_matrix DPAS tiles (8x16x16 half, F32 accumulate, online softmax in F32). The cell list is
compacted in a stream (a cell listed twice counts once, as in the mask). GGML_SYCL_SPF_MIN_KV: below this n_kv the
dense path runs (it is cheaper per call there); GGML_SYCL_SPF_MIN_T (default 256): chunks of fewer queries (decode and
verify steps, short turns over a long cache) leave it too. GGML_SYCL_SPF_CHECK=1 runs both and compares per layer;
GGML_SYCL_SPF_DEBUG=1 reports where the matcher stops.

